{
  "format": "dive-shared-table-layout-v1",
  "source": "tlaplus/Examples 6a7b26a31c1a6aeec789b455e9bbfa3b3ad2728f, specifications/KeyValueStore; original transitions except explicitly named Corrupt. Removed SYMMETRY TxIdSymmetric from the selected CFG in every labeled trial. Kept TxIdSymmetric == Permutations(TxId) in the TLA+ file. V=2 throughout.",
  "method": "Isolated AWS EC2 c7i.4xlarge, Ubuntu 24.04.5, Intel Xeon Platinum 8488C, 8 physical cores and 16 vCPUs. Fresh processes pinned to separate physical cores; several jobs ran concurrently. Wall seconds and child/process peak RSS KiB from GNU time. Main CLI/exporter rebuilt from 901f533e, release with LTO disabled. Both arms of the paired shipping comparison use identical executables. The Python worker is the only arm difference.",
  "commands": [
    "python3 scripts/perf/scale/sail_kvs_edits.py KVS OUT --keys K --transactions T",
    "sed '/^SYMMETRY$/{N;d;}' OUT/CASE/Model.cfg > labeled.cfg",
    "dive check OUT/CASE/MCKVS.tla --config labeled.cfg --strategy symbolic --time-limit SECONDS --output json",
    "For induction add --prove-inductive and use CASE=FullHasFresh; retain TypeInvariant, TxLifecycle, FullHasFresh and SomeCommit. The unchanged relation is always checked from source. Replaying a stored predicate uses the search encoding."
  ],
  "roles": {
    "base": "Complete labeled BFS of the original TypeInvariant and TxLifecycle configuration.",
